Description: Reads the cards of 'AudioMoth' recorders (Hill et al. 2018)
    <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.12955> ('CONFIG.TXT' file and daily folders),
    optionally copies them to the disk, prepares the audio and analyses it
    with 'BirdNET' (Kahl et al. 2021) <doi:10.1016/j.ecoinf.2021.101236>
    through 'birdnetR', with the species expected at the site or an own
    list of species (which can be built from the observations published in
    'GBIF' around the recorder). Saves the
    detections as CSV files, extracts high-confidence examples of the chosen
    species with their audio and a video of the spectrogram, creates a web
    page to validate the records by ear, and converts the detections into
    the import format of 'Observation.org', translating the species names
    into the IOC World Bird List. It also creates a PDF report with 'Quarto'
    of one or several recorders, with a map, the state of the recordings and
    the detected species.
